 "units": "cm (h, 1.20/2.20/0.88 m on GP220 sheet); volume m3 ('Volum (mc)'); mass kg",
 "method": "Each section is the catalogue's filled vector outline (PDF p3/p4, the schematic next to each table), digitised from the PDF path (Bezier arcs sampled at 12 chords) in points, re-centred, and scaled to the printed depth h. The schematics are drawn to scale: the IPTANA GP42 and GP72 icons scaled this way reproduce the separately dimensioned ASA IPTANA 42/72 outlines (width/depth 1.43 and 1.42) and the Somaco volume/length within 0-2%. GP220-40 section E-E is scaled separately in x (printed 1.20 m top / 0.88 m bottom) and y (printed 2.20 m) because its drawing is 4% compressed vertically.",
 "geometry_notes": [
  "Schematic outlines only: no widths/thicknesses are printed except GP220 (1.20 top, 0.88 bottom, 2.20 depth). All other dimensions are scaled: ESTIMATE.",
  "The icon beside the Eurocod I table (GP 85E/95E/105E) scaled to h=105 matches GP105E volume/length exactly (0.533 m2); scaled to h=95 it gives -9% vs 0.479 m2; GP85E (0.234 m2) is clearly a different shape and is NOT implemented.",
  "GP93 T (IPTANA table) scaled to h=93 gives 0.305 m2 vs V/L 0.316 m2 (-3.4%). Its scaled widths (top 1200, bottom 450, web 160) coincide with the dimensioned ASA 'grindă pod 95' section, but the depth printed by Somaco is 93 cm; kept as a separate Somaco estimate.",
  "GP 42/52/72/80 (IPTANA) are not implemented here: they are the IPTANA sections already implemented from the dimensioned ASA CONS catalogue (bridgebeams.ro.asa). Somaco V/L cross-checks them: 42 0.130-0.133 vs ASA 0.132; 52 0.150 vs 0.154; 72 0.386 vs 0.389; 80 0.407 vs 0.411 m2.",
  "Handling anchors (Ancora manipulare), strands and GP220 end section D-D are excluded; GP220 V/L 0.871 m2 includes the thickened end zones, so the midspan E-E area (0.72 m2) is lower.",
  "Outline is the raw digitised path (not symmetrised); left/right asymmetry < 0.5 pt (~5 mm).",
  "GP 52E scales to exactly the ASA/IPTANA 52 envelope (600 bottom, 220 top) but with a thicker stem (194 vs 176 mm at mid-depth), consistent with its larger V/L (0.178 vs 0.150 m2)."
 ],
